<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian raw sugar exports ease in 1995/96.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian raw sugar exports ease in 1995/96.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian raw sugar exports eased 4.6 percent to 3.79 million tonnes actual in 1995/96 ended June 30 from the record 3.97 million tonnes shipped in 1994/95 due to increased sales to Australian refiners, Queensland Sugar Corp (QSC) said.</p>
<p>Canada replaced Japan as its leading market in the latest year, QSC said in its 1995/96 annual report.</p>
<p>QSC's third largest export customer was Malaysia, followed by South Korea, the annual report shows.</p>
<p>Sales to China fell sharply in the latest year.</p>
<p>QSC handles all Australia's raw sugar exports.  </p>
